              <p>
                The consequence for tooling is immediate. A stamping die is a
                punch-and-die pair that has to survive impact thousands of times
                without its edge rolling over. A casting mold is a cavity that has
                to survive heat, pressure and abrasive alloy without its surface
                eroding. Two different tools, two different failure modes, two
                different maintenance routines.
              </p>
            </section>

            <!-- ---------- 02 ---------- -->
            <section
              id="tooling"
